[list]
[*]New mod setting, Keep colonists decent, off by default. Turn it on and a stand will not leave a colonist without basic clothing: if what it hands out does not cover them, their innermost garments stay on and the rest of the swap happens as normal. The innermost layers are the ones kept, so a shirt and trousers stay put while a parka or a duster goes into storage.
[*]It is off by default on purpose. Nothing changes in a colony you are already playing unless you switch it on, which matters most if you got this mod as part of a pack.
[*]It shows up mainly with Change the whole outfit ticked. That setting takes off everything the colonist arrived in, so a stand holding only a hat, a belt or a pair of trousers sends them out with nothing else on. With the new setting enabled they keep what they need instead.
[*]What gets held back depends on the colonist. RimWorld asks for trousers on everyone and a covered torso as well on women, so the same stand with the same setting can keep a shirt on one colonist and not on another.
[*]Nudists, and anyone whose ideoligion prefers nudity, are never affected. For them being dressed is the penalty, so nothing is held back whatever the setting says. This follows the same rule the game uses when deciding whether to put clothes on a prisoner.
[/list]
